<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Uncalibrated Non-Uniform Quantization</h3>

<figure id="S3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Weight-only uncalibrated PTQ on Qwen3 models with 4-bit non-uniform quantization, reporting perplexity and actual memory usage (GB). Lower is better for all metrics.
The best <em id="S3.T4.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">non-uniform</em> result for a given setting is marked in <span id="S3.T4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>, the results where SINQ with uniform quantization outperforms the non-uniform baselines are marked <span id="S3.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">red</span>.</figcaption>
