<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Results on Llama Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.3 Results on Llama Models ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ SINQ: Sinkhorn-Normalized Quantization for Calibration-Free Low-Precision LLM Weights" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> we report quantization results on Llama family models. These findings further validate the effectiveness of SINQ also on this type of architecture.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Weight-only PTQ on Llama models with 3-bit and 4-bit quantization, reporting perplexity and actual memory usage (GB). Lower is better for all metrics. In bold is the best result for a given setting. </figcaption>
