<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Results on DeepSeek-V3</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Tab. <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.4 Results on DeepSeek-V3 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ SINQ: Sinkhorn-Normalized Quantization for Calibration-Free Low-Precision LLM Weights" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> we compare HQQ to SINQ on WikiText2 perplexity for DeepSeek-V3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Weight-only PTQ on <span id="A1.T9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepSeek-V3-685B</span> with 4-bit quantization.
We report perplexity on WikiText-2 (lower is better). Best per setting in <span id="A1.T9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T9.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T9.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
